From: Cyrus Lien <cyrus.lien@canonical.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 03:08:48 +0800
Subject: system,
 users: Keep fingerprint add-print popover visible when scaled

When configuring Fingerprint Login on small or tablet displays,
especially at 200% display scaling, clicking "Scan new fingerprint" can
produce no visible response. The finger-list popover is too tall to fit
below the button, GTK cannot place it above either, and the popover
fails to appear, blocking the user from selecting a finger to enroll.

Track the add-print button and choose the popover position by available
room. Wrap the popover content in a scrolled window so the popup can stay
visible when vertical space is limited.

Bug-Ubuntu: https://launchpad.net/bugs/2158603
Forwarded: not-needed

Upstream is working on redesign fingerprint management interface:
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-control-center/-/merge_requests/3399
---
 panels/system/users/cc-fingerprint-dialog.blp |  12 +-
 panels/system/users/cc-fingerprint-dialog.c   | 166 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 174 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/panels/system/users/cc-fingerprint-dialog.blp b/panels/system/users/cc-fingerprint-dialog.blp
index ffb7b9b..4744283 100644
--- a/panels/system/users/cc-fingerprint-dialog.blp
+++ b/panels/system/users/cc-fingerprint-dialog.blp
@@ -250,9 +250,15 @@ template $CcFingerprintDialog: Adw.Dialog {
 Popover add_print_popover {
   position: bottom;
 
-  Box add_print_popover_box {
+  ScrolledWindow add_print_popover_scroller {
     can-focus: false;
-    spacing: 6;
-    orientation: vertical;
+    hscrollbar-policy: never;
+    propagate-natural-height: true;
+
+    Box add_print_popover_box {
+      can-focus: false;
+      spacing: 6;
+      orientation: vertical;
+    }
   }
 }
